% =========================================================================
% SCRIPT: Analyze Neural Activity Time-Locked to Sleep Spindles (SWS)
% SUBJECT: Mouse12-120807
% =========================================================================
% DESCRIPTION:
% This script analyzes LFP and spike train data during Slow-Wave Sleep.
% It aligns neural activity to detected Sleep Spindles (All, Global, and 
% Local) to compute population averages (mean LFP, raster, firing rate) 
% and performs single-cell analysis to calculate a Modulation Index 
% (peak-to-trough firing rate difference) for each neuron.
%
% INPUTS:
%   - SpikesSWS120807.mat: Spike data during slow-wave sleep.
%   - sepratedSpindles120807.mat: Spindle events (global/local peaks).
%   - thal_ch_norm_filtered_120807.mat: Filtered thalamic LFP data.
%   - Mouse12-120807.spikes.cellinfo.mat: Cell metadata.
%   - real_peaks_120807[X].mat: Real peaks for the reference channel.
%
% OUTPUTS:
%   - 3 Population Figures (All, Global, Local spindles):
%       1. Mean raw LFP waveform.
%       2. Spike raster plot.
%       3. Smoothed population firing rate.
%   - FiringrateSpindles.mat: Population firing rates (Global/Local).
%   - ModuIndex.mat: Single-cell modulation indices (Global/Local).
%
% DEPENDENCIES:
%   - Custom functions: SpikeRaster, getShankID, findThroughs, findMaxPeak
% =========================================================================

